# The blocking subset.
#
# THREE LEVELS, added 2026-08-24. They mean different things and must not be conflated:
#
#   blocking execution      Must hold for the current pipeline to run. Listed below; the
#                           pre-commit hook and CI enforce them.
#   advisory historical     Cannot be made green because a historical input is genuinely gone.
#                           test-matching-provenance.R is the case: the gazetteer build the
#                           cohort was matched against was overwritten and cannot be recovered,
#                           and control_candidates_raw.csv carries no coordinates.
#   See docs/SCIENTIFIC_CI_LAWS.md for the two laws every scientific contract must satisfy:
#   a positive and a negative control, and independent confirmation of any result that could
#   change the frozen cohort.
#
#   NOT YET LISTED, with a stated trigger: test-fielded-frame-eligibility.R holds the two laws
#   the corrected frame must satisfy -- no Eligible = FALSE clinician in a fielded frame, and
#   the frame must be a subset of the POST-EXCLUSION eligible universe, pairs included. It
#   fails today by design (45 ineligible, 173 outside the universe, 147 pairs that do not
#   exist there). It is advisory only because promoting it now would block the commits that
#   fix it. PROMOTE IT the moment a corrected frame is generated; it is the regression test
#   for Finding C and would have prevented it.
#
#   publication readiness   Does not stop data collection, but must block any claim that the
#                           cohort is fully reproducible, and must block final manuscript
#                           release unless resolved or disclosed. See docs/MATCHING_LINEAGE.md
#                           findings B and C.
#
# These test files must pass before a commit lands. The rest of the suite is advisory until it
# is clean; a gate you routinely bypass is not a gate, so this list starts with the files that
# are green and grows as others are fixed. Promotion is a one-line edit here.
#
# Format: <needs-data> <file>
#   data  - reads a cohort CSV, so it can only run where the (gitignored) data is present
#   nodata- runs anywhere, including CI
#
# RESOLVED 2026-08-11: the gazetteer question, split in two.
#   test-geocode-lookup.R is gone. It conflated two questions and pinned the pipeline to a
#   dependency's storage schema, which is precisely what broke when mysterycall renamed its
#   columns. It is replaced by:
#
#     test-frozen-geo-reference.R      BLOCKING. The coordinate set the fielded cohort's
#                                      10-mile caliper actually used is immutable, hashed, and
#                                      covers every fielded clinician.
#     test-gazetteer-compatibility.R   NON-BLOCKING. Can the CURRENT mysterycall gazetteer be
#                                      normalised to the four-column pipeline contract? A pass
#                                      does NOT license substituting it into the primary
#                                      analysis.
#
#   The mysterycall build used to construct the cohort could not be reconstructed and no longer
#   exists. Re-resolving through the current build reproduces 82.2% of the persisted
#   coordinates, max discrepancy 54 degrees. See inst/frozen/PROVENANCE.md.
#
# Files deliberately NOT yet blocking.
#   test-matching-provenance.R is NOT promoted, deliberately: its control-candidate contract
#   documents a blocker that cannot be closed with data this repository contains --
#   control_candidates_raw.csv has no coordinates, so the 10-mile caliper never fired.
#   Its other contracts are green and mutation-proven. Promote it when that input exists.
#
#   STALE, corrected 2026-08-28 (per ~/CI_BEST_PRACTICES.md item 9 -- re-verify "as of DATE"
#   claims rather than propagate them): this list used to name a per-file failure count "as of
#   2026-08-10". Spot-checking test-table1-balance.R against that claim on 2026-08-28 found it
#   no longer matches -- the file now errors before producing the 12 individual failures the
#   comment names, consistent with the file itself having changed in the 2026-08-23/24 merge,
#   not with the count being re-measured and confirmed. The other counts below were not
#   independently re-verified (this machine has no gitignored cohort data to run them against)
#   and must not be read as current. Re-run each file listed below with the real cohort data
#   present before trusting any number attached to it; test-taxonomy-eligibility.R was already
#   confirmed promoted (2026-08-24, green at 27 assertions) and is not in this list.
